{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Revata of the Acacia Wood","html":"<article id='thag1.42'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.42 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.42 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Pañcamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Five </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Khadiravaniyattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Revata of the Acacia Wood </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Cāle upacāle sīsūpacāle (…), </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Cālā, Upacālā, Sīsupacālā— </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Patissatā nu kho viharatha; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>meditate mindfully! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Āgato vo vālaṁ viya vedhī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve come to you like a hair-splitter. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Khadiravaniyo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
